.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
m4
- the macro processor
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
m4 [ file ... ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
M4 is a general-purpose macro processor.  Each file is processed in
order; with none, or with an argument of -, standard input is read and
the result written to standard output.  A macro call is name(arg1, ...,
argn); the left parenthesis must follow the name with no space, and a
defined name with no parenthesis is taken to have no arguments.  Left
and right single quotes, ` and ', quote strings; the value of a quoted
string is the string without the quotes.
.sp
A macro value may name its arguments $1 through $9; at expansion they
are replaced by the actuals.  The builtins are:
.sp
.in +5
.br
.bd
define(name, value)
.sp
define a new macro, or redefine one.
.br
.bd
undefine(name)
.sp
remove a definition.
.br
.bd
ifdef(name, yes, no)
.sp
expand yes if name is defined, no otherwise.
.br
.bd
ifelse(a, b, yes, ...)
.sp
expand yes if a and b are equal, else the next triple, else the last
argument.
.br
.bd
len(s)
.sp
the length of s.
.br
.bd
substr(s, i, n)
.sp
the substring of s at i of length n.
.br
.bd
index(s, t)
.sp
the position of t in s, or -1.
.br
.bd
translit(s, from, to)
.sp
translate the characters of s named in from to those in to.
.br
.bd
incr(n)
.sp
the value of n plus one.
.br
.bd
eval(expr)
.sp
the value of the arithmetic expression expr.
.br
.bd
changequote(l, r)
.sp
change the quote characters; with no arguments, restore ` and '.
.br
.bd
include(file)
.br
.bd
sinclude(file)
.sp
read file; include is an error if it is missing, sinclude is not.
.br
.bd
syscmd(cmd)
.sp
hand cmd to the shell.
.br
.bd
maketemp(template)
.sp
a unique name built from the template's XXXXXX.
.br
.bd
divert(n)
.br
.bd
undivert(n)
.br
.bd
divnum
.sp
divert output to a numbered stream, bring it back, or print the current
stream number.
.br
.bd
dnl
.sp
delete the rest of the line.
.br
.bd
dumpdef(name ...)
.sp
print definitions to standard error.
.br
.bd
errprint(message)
.sp
print to standard error.
.in -5
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
